---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DraftNotice from "../components/DraftNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Make Money"
  description="This site currently makes no money. Any future referral or advertising relationship will be clearly disclosed."
>
  <DraftNotice
    note="This page is a draft and has not yet been reviewed by an insurance-regulatory lawyer. Wording may change before this site is used publicly."
  />
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>How We Make Money</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Right now, this site makes no money. There are no ads, no referral
      fees, no sponsored placements, and we don't sell your information to
      anyone — because we don't collect it in the first place (see our
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page).
    </p>

    <h2>If that changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may explore ways to fund this project in the future — for example,
      referral relationships with licensed insurance agencies or carriers,
      clearly labeled advertising, or an affiliate/comparison arrangement
      where legally and contractually permitted. None of these are active
      today.
    </p>
    <p>If any of them launch in the future, we commit to the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Any commercial relationship that could influence what you see will be
        clearly and separately disclosed, in plain language, on the page
        where it applies.
      </li>
      <li>
        A referral or advertiser relationship will never change which facts
        we verify or how a fact is displayed — the same "primary source,
        current, or it doesn't get published" rule applies regardless of who
        is or isn't paying us.
      </li>
      <li>
        We will not launch a quote, lead-collection, or referral feature
        without first reviewing it with an insurance-regulatory lawyer.
      </li>
      <li>
        We will not label a company "best" or "recommended" without a
        transparent, published methodology behind that label.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Questions about this? See <a href="/about/">About</a> or our
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
